# Onboard parameters for Vehicle 1
#
# STAGE 3a - HEIGHT. Independent of vision, UART and the container.
#
# Range finder as the height reference, barometer as backup: PX4 v1.16's documented
# "Indoor (non-flat terrain)" configuration -- GPS_CTRL 0, BARO_CTRL 1, RNG_CTRL 1
# (conditional), HGT_REF 2 (range). Source: docs.px4.io/v1.16/en/advanced_config/
# tuning_the_ecl_ekf.html, "Height". Non-flat because the course may have boxes and
# tables: in conditional mode the range finder is only fused at low speed
# (< EKF2_RNG_A_VMAX, 1 m/s) and low height (< EKF2_RNG_A_HMAX), with a consistency
# gate on height-above-ground (EKF2_RNG_A_IGATE); otherwise PX4 "automatically
# selects a secondary reference" -- the barometer. For a guaranteed-flat floor PX4's
# "Indoor (flat terrain)" variant is EKF2_RNG_CTRL = 2 (always).
#
# The range finder is the ST VL53L1X: the PX4 driver's maximum is 4 m (long mode,
# less in bright light), 27 deg field of view, one reading per 200 ms. Hence
# EKF2_RNG_A_HMAX = 3 m, inside that range, and a matching GF_MAX_VER_DIST on each
# drone (see fleet/<serial>-fixes-*.params).
#
# The runaway climb this replaces: the May-07 airframe had HGT_REF = 2 (range),
# BARO_CTRL = 0 and GPS off. Whenever the range finder stopped delivering (above
# its range, over an obstacle, a rejected sample) there was NO height source left;
# the estimate free-ran, the controller read it as sinking and climbed forever.
# The essential fix is BARO_CTRL = 1: with a second source PX4 "continues to
# estimate its height using the other sensors". (EKF2_RNG_A_HMAX, blamed for this
# until 2026-10-15, only applies in conditional mode.)
#
# Caveat from the same PX4 page: switching between height references makes the
# absolute altitude estimate drift over time.
#
# After loading: reboot the FC, then the props-off and hand-lift checks of
# docs/fleet_guide.md step 6 before any hover.
#
# Vehicle-Id	Component-Id	Name	Value	Type
1	1	EKF2_HGT_REF	2	6
1	1	EKF2_BARO_CTRL	1	6
1	1	EKF2_RNG_CTRL	1	6
1	1	EKF2_RNG_A_HMAX	3.000000	9
1	1	EKF2_GPS_CTRL	0	6
